{"study_accession":"PRJNA509151","secondary_study_accession":"SRP173218","title":"Genome-wide RNA-seq and ATAC-seq analysis of an in vivo human immune response to acute Zika virus infection","description":"A longitudinal systems immunologic investigation of acute Zika virus infection in an individual infected with ZIKV while traveling to Caracas, Venezuela during the zika virus epidemic. Includes longitudinal RNA-seq and ATAC-seq characterization of innate and adaptive immune responses during an acute ZIKV infection. Overall design: Blood was collected from an individual with NAAT confirmed acute Zika virus infection on four occasions d3, d6, d17, and d48 post-onset of symptoms (POS). Peripheral blood mononuclear cells were isolated from heparinized blood using Histopaque-1077 per manufacturers instructions and subjected to flow activated cell sorting (FACS) to characterize and isolate innate and adaptive immune cell populations. 5000-15,000 live PBMCs or individual cell populations were used to perform low input RNA-seq using the Smart-seq2 method with some modifications. 50,000 FACS isolated live classical monocytes or NK cells were used for ATAC-seq analysis.","pubmed":"30596671","geo_series":"","n_samples":35,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN10564219","study_accession":"PRJNA509151","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"CD14posCD16neg-Day48","description":"CD14posCD16neg-Day48","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3506306","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2018-12-22","attributes":[["source_name","CD14posCD16neg monocyte"],["subject status","individual with NAAT confirmed acute Zika virus infection"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["cell_subtype","CD14posCD16neg monocyte"],["time post onset of symptoms","48 days"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR8309270","experiment_accession":"SRX5123200","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2000","read_count":38240933,"base_count":1912046650,"first_public":"2018-